<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes, or T-bill, rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said on Monday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	21.45	    - 46	    21.00     21.68</p>
<p>91-Day	23.21	    - 29	    23.00     23.28</p>
<p>182-Day     24.06	    - 10	    24.00     24.12</p>
<p>363-Day     25.30				24.90     25.37</p>
<p>Last week the 335-day paper was assigned at 25.68 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.28 bln pesos     2.54</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   2.57 bln pesos     2.86</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   4.08 bln pesos     4.53</p>
<p>363-Day     600 million pesos   3.79 bln pesos     6.32</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.85 on demand of 12.72 billion pesos compared with 4.36 the week before, on demand of 14.38 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  23  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   7  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  6  basis points</p>
<p>    363-Day			  7  basis points</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
